# p-drag (M9): P dragged along the curve (FunctionViewer.tsx's onMarkDrag: P's x follows the pointer,
# its y keeps to the curve). P (2.00, 4.00) on x² at (1056, 288) at 1440 x 900; the pointer on its
# 48 px box names it (Q hides) and shows the open hand; pressed and moved 50 px left over 160 ms, P
# moves as far as the pointer went along x, to P (1.00, 1.00) at (1006, 438), lit while it drags (its
# halo, its drop lines, its row), Q hidden, the closed hand. Let go, the plane says nothing more until
# the pointer moves (React's endMarkDrag reports nothing), so P stays named under the open hand.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 1056 288
wait 500
shot over-p
down
move 1006 288 over 160
wait 16
shot dragging
up
wait 500
shot released
